**Known issues and warnings:** Collisions can occur with rests, when using `\cueDuring`, between `Voice` and `CueVoice` contexts.  When using `\cueDuringWithClef` or `\transposedCueDuring` the extra argument required for each case must come after the quote and the direction.

Fingering instructions can be entered using `<note>-<digit>`:

Example (renders in Score Chat):
```lilypond
\version "2.24.4"
\score {
\new Staff {
\relative { c''4-1 d-2 f-4 e-3 }
}
}
```

Markup texts or strings may be used for finger changes.

Example (not supported by the Score Chat renderer):
```lilypond
\version "2.24.4"
\relative {
  c''4-1 d-2 f\finger \markup \tied-lyric "4~3" c\finger "2 - 3"
}
```

A thumb fingering can be added (e.g., cello music) to indicate that a note should be played with the thumb.

Example (not supported by the Score Chat renderer):
```lilypond
\version "2.24.4"
\relative { <a'_\thumb a'-3>2 <b_\thumb b'-3> }
```

Fingerings for chords can also be added to individual notes by adding them after the pitches.

Example (renders in Score Chat):
```lilypond
\version "2.24.4"
\score {
\new Staff {
\relative {
  <c''-1 e-2 g-3 b-5>2 <d-1 f-2 a-3 c-5>
}
}
}
```

Fingering instructions may be manually placed above or below the staff, see “Direction and placement”.

